{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01PWCdpMMV1pdTjKXtgPoB7Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **Q29: Human-in-the-loop patterns — when trigger human review?**\n\nKey content in `03-029-human-in-the-loop-patterns-when-trigger-human-review.md`:\n\n- **4 trigger categories** (all implemented as orchestrator-side code, not LLM prompts):\n  1. **Irreversibility** — send/delete/payment → `interrupt_before` in LangGraph\n  2. **Confidence below threshold** — structured `CLARIFY` action type\n  3. **High-stakes domain** — static allowlist of tool+context combinations\n  4. **Budget/anomaly** — orchestrator circuit-breaker (2× token spend, turn count > 80% of max)\n\n- **Tiered autonomy model**: synchronous approval (irreversible) → async shadow review (undo-able writes) → fully autonomous (reads/drafts)\n\n- **Trust-escalation pattern**: track which synchronous interrupts are 100% approved → promote to async → eventually autonomous\n\n- **Key pitfalls**: putting HITL in prompts instead of orchestrator code; applying HITL everywhere without considering latency; not checkpointing state before interrupts\n\n10 questions remain in the Next queue."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":365,"cache_read_input_tokens":64564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":365,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b783a29b-8d00-40d1-ae5e-bf44b190070a","uuid":"9a4046b6-7fdd-4744-b172-c23be20f96fa"}
